{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A Wi-Fi router broadcasts a signal in a circular pattern. The radius (in meters) grows according to the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7912c0e7e292381943e2148fd42a8b166f5091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(t)=2t+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is time in minutes. What is the area of signal coverage after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c913cff7776ae19bed793a777bfc7157591527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> minutes?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d7b31b02dc51be47cca6878e8516907a4f19d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  10\\text{ m}^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  20\\pi\\text{ m} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  20\\pi\\text{ m}^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  100\\pi\\text{ m} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  100\\pi\\text{ m}^2 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"611\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>According to the function, the radius at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319e057adf4ab6c7e854a57e87af23f2abc5a65e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 + 4 = 6 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e395842e51bdc8b415b4e4639a2abc265d07bebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />. The area of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c935c7f548efe289af81b189b5ee3d0bd940207a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\times r^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the radius of the circle. This means that the area of the circle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826c5eeb5c243d9d03257f27e8b6235968a2aad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\times 10^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef566d4ccd6caed5d7d93f0120ad0a373fd822c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 100\\pi\\text{ m}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"112\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Proble